 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Cause with из-за",
     "texto": [
      "**Из-за + genitive** means «because of»: **из-за пробки**, **из-за дождя**. It usually appears with an obstacle or an unfavourable result, but the nuance depends on the context.",
      "**Мы опоздали из-за пробки** («We were late because of the traffic jam»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Cause with a clause: так как",
     "texto": [
      "**Так как** and **потому что** introduce a full clause and express cause. **Так как** can come at the beginning, as here: **Так как была авария, все стояли** («As there was an accident, everyone was standing still»). There is no fixed difference in formality between the two connectors.",
      "**Поскольку** also expresses cause («since», «as»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Usual favourable cause: благодаря",
     "texto": [
      "**Благодаря + dative** means «thanks to» and normally introduces a favourable cause: **благодаря тебе**, **благодаря друзьям**. The contrast with **из-за** is a tendency, not an absolute rule."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
